      "hints": [
        "Apply $S_n = \\frac{a(r^n - 1)}{r - 1}$ with $a = p, r = 2$ to get $p(2^n - 1) > 1000p$.",
        "Divide by $p$ and show $2^n > 1001$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Identify the parameters of the geometric progression: first term $a = p$, common ratio $r = \\frac{2p}{p} = 2$.",
        "Write the sum formula for the first $n$ terms:\n$$S_n = \\frac{p(2^n - 1)}{2 - 1} = p(2^n - 1)$$",
        "Set up the given inequality $S_n > 1000p$ and divide by the positive constant $p$:\n$$p(2^n - 1) > 1000p \\implies 2^n - 1 > 1000 \\implies 2^n > 1001$$"
      ],
