      "hints": [
        "For AP with $a = p, d = p$: $u_n = np = 336$ and $S_n = \\frac{n}{2}(p + np) = 7224$.",
        "Substitute $np = 336$ into $S_n$ to find $n = 42$ and $p = 8$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "For the arithmetic progression with first term $a = p$ and common difference $d = 2p - p = p$, set up the $n$th term and sum equations:\n$$u_n = p + (n - 1)p = np = 336$$\n$$S_n = \\frac{n}{2}[2p + (n - 1)p] = \\frac{n}{2}(p + np) = 7224$$",
        "Substitute $np = 336$ into the sum equation:\n$$\\frac{n}{2}(p + 336) = \\frac{np + 336n}{2} = \\frac{336 + 336n}{2} = 168(1 + n) = 7224$$",
        "Solve for $n$:\n$$1 + n = \\frac{7224}{168} = 43 \\implies n = 42$$",
        "Substitute $n = 42$ into $np = 336$ to find $p$:\n$$p = \\frac{336}{42} = 8$$"
      ],
